    "body": "`DataAnalyzer.run_map` fills the process list in the order of `threads_to_run` but starts and joins with `p[thread]`, so `specific_threads` only works when it is `[0, 1, ..., k]`. Anything else, like `[2, 3]` to rerun two failed threads, raises `IndexError: list index out of range`.\n\nFix: start the process that was just appended (`p[-1]`) and join over `p` directly. Two lines.\n\nTest: `test_data_analyzer_runs_only_the_specific_threads` runs `run_map` with `num_threads=4, specific_threads=[2, 3]` and checks that only `worker0_thread2` and `worker0_thread3` are written, holding samples 10 to 14 and 15 to 19. It fails on master with the IndexError and passes with the fix. `pytest tests/unit/runtime/test_data_efficiency.py`: 15 passed, 2 skipped (the two-GPU curriculum tests). Run on an M-series Mac, CPU only, torch 2.14.0. pre-commit passes on both changed files.\n\nThis doesn't touch the `len(data)` sample counting in the same file, which #8505 already covers.\n\nFixes #8757\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
    "closed_at": "2026-10-09T13:22:08Z",
